problem:
`push_base_lines` copies base's last line as it is, even when it has no final newline, and settled disk lines follow it, so two lines join. Example: base `{
  "a": 1
}` (no EOF newline), ours/theirs adding `"x"`/`"y"` before a shared `}
` (git leaves `}` settled after the block). The middle comes out as `…  "a": 1
}}
`, `line_count` says one line more than the text has, every later middle range is off by one, and applying ours over middle {2,2} drops the closing `}`.

#923 `state.toText(reply.result)` splits only on the pane's separator, so in a CRLF Result an LF answer from the formatter stays one 'line' full of `
` characters. Node: `toText("a;
b;
")` with separator `
` gives `["a;
b;
"]`, `lines: 1`. LF is the default line ending of prettier-style formatters [INFERENCE for oxfmt]. The result is a doc whose lines contain line breaks, one line number, every open block collapsed to ignored, and `resultText()` returning LF, so the CRLF file is rewritten to LF. The CRLF tests only feed results that are already CRLF.

